WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Our episodes deal with serious and often distressing incidents. If you feel at any time you need support, please contact your local crisis centre. For suggested phone numbers for confidential support, please see the show notes for this episode on your app or on our website. This episode involves a crime against children. It may not be suitable for all listeners. February 5, 1921 was far from a typical Saturday afternoon in the valley town of Abbottoliri, Wales.
我们的节目涉及严重且往往令人痛心的事件。如果您在任何时候感到需要支持，请联系您当地的危机中心。有关保密支持的建议电话号码，请查看您使用的应用程序或我们网站上的本期节目说明。本期节目涉及针对儿童的犯罪。可能不适合所有听众。1921年2月5日，对威尔士阿伯泰勒里（Abbottoliri）山谷小镇来说，绝不是一个平常的星期六下午。

2
00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Locals had rallied together to undertake a desperate search. Crescent residences along the main street were checked, as were the narrow alleyways between them. Men and their sons ventured off into the surrounding hills, while others trekked the lengths of the railway tracks and the nearby Ebor River. Their efforts were in vain. But they didn't give up. As the dull skies gave way to night, people were still searching.
当地人联合起来展开了一场绝望的搜寻。主街沿线的住宅受到了检查，它们之间的狭窄小巷也是如此。男人和他们的儿子们冒险进入周围的山丘，而其他人则沿着铁路线和附近的埃博尔河（Ebor River）上下搜寻。他们的努力是徒劳的。但他们并没有放弃。随着阴沉的天空逐渐变黑，人们仍在搜寻。

3
00:01:22.000 --> 00:02:22.000
They were joined by the town crier, who paraded up and down the main street, shouting the name of the eight-year-old girl who had vanished from town that morning. Freed up, Bernel. Freed up, Bernel. Hours earlier, Freed up, Bernel had been skipping down Somerset Street into Abbottoliri's bustling town centre. The side of little Freed up, in her black buttoned boots, red cap and brown coat, all by herself, didn't raise any eyebrows.
镇上的传令官加入了他们的行列，他在主街上游行，大声喊着那个那天早上在镇上失踪的八岁女孩的名字。弗里达·伯内尔（Freed up, Bernel）。弗里达·伯内尔。几小时前，弗里达·伯内尔还蹦蹦跳跳地顺着萨默塞特街（Somerset Street）走入阿伯泰勒里繁华的市中心。小弗里达穿着黑色纽扣靴、戴着红帽子、穿着棕色大衣，独自一人，并没有引起任何人的注意。

4
00:02:22.000 --> 00:03:03.000
The coal mining town she called home was small, and the locals trusted each other. Freed up was running an errand for her father, who was in need of some feed and poultry grit for the chickens they owned. He had promised his daughter a penny as a reward for buying the supplies on his behalf. At around 9am, the bell at the top of the front door of Mortimer's store jingled as Freed up entered. The shop specialised in livestock supplies, and while they had the chicken feed Freed up requested, there weren't any sacks of grit, only loose grit.
她称之为家的这个煤矿小镇很小，当地人彼此信任。弗里达正在为父亲跑腿，父亲需要一些他们养的鸡吃的饲料和家禽砂砾。他曾承诺女儿，如果她代为买回这些物资，就奖励她一分钱。大约上午9点，当弗里达走进莫蒂默（Mortimer's）商店时，前门顶部的铃铛叮当作响。这家商店专门经营牲畜用品，虽然他们有弗里达要求的鸡饲料，但没有任何袋装砂砾，只有散装砂砾。

5
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:40.000
Freed up said she would go home to ask her father if that would suffice, and if so, she would come back. But she never returned. By late afternoon, Abbottoliri's locals were assisting police and the Bernel family in trying to locate Freed up. Somehow, during her journey home from Mortimer's store, she had vanished without a trace. The following morning, a local coal worker finished his shift in the mines and began the walk back to his home.
弗里达说她要回家问问父亲这样是否可以，如果可以，她会再回来。但她再也没有回来。到傍晚时分，阿伯泰勒里的当地人正协助警察和伯内尔一家寻找弗里达。不知何故，在她从莫蒂默商店回家的路上，她消失得无影无踪。第二天早上，当地的一名煤矿工人在矿上结束了夜班，开始步行回家。

6
00:03:40.000 --> 00:04:19.000
As he approached Abbottoliri's town centre, he headed down a narrow side alley, where he stumbled across a Hessian sack discarded in the mud. It clearly held something. The coal worker examined the sack closely. Inside was the body of 8-year-old Freed up Bernel. Her remains had been dumped just 90 metres from her house. Freed up had sustained a violent blow to the head, but it was the cord still wrapped around her neck that had caused her death.
当他走近阿伯泰勒里市中心时，他走进了一条狭窄的小巷，在那里他无意中发现了泥地里丢弃的一个麻袋。里面显然装着东西。煤矿工人仔细检查了这个麻袋。里面是8岁女孩弗里达·伯内尔的尸体。她的遗体被抛弃在距离她家仅90米的地方。弗里达头部遭受了猛烈的撞击，但真正导致她死亡的是缠在她脖子上的绳索。

7
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:58.000
A piece of cloth was stuffed inside her mouth, and her wrists and ankles were tied behind her back with rope. Her attacker had also attempted to rape her. The shocking murder rattled the typically carefree townsfolk. Freed's funeral was held on the street outside her home to facilitate the large crowds of mourners that wished to attend. They circled around her small coffin, their sense of loss tinged with fear as they wondered who among them would carry out such a violent and disturbing crime.
她嘴里塞着一块布，手腕和脚踝用绳子反绑在身后。她的袭击者还试图强奸她。这起令人震惊的谋杀案震惊了平时无忧无虑的镇民。弗里达的葬礼在她家门外的街道上举行，以便容纳希望参加的大批哀悼者。他们围在她的小棺材周围，失落感中夹杂着恐惧，他们想知道他们当中究竟是谁犯下了如此暴力和令人不安的罪行。

8
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:37.000
In a desperate bid to identify Freed's killer, locals carried out a seance. In the 1920s, it was widely believed that such acts allowed communication with spirits who might be able to provide crucial information. According to one participant, the seance succeeded, with the spirits offering a description of Freed's murderer. This description just so happened to match that of a man seen loitering near the alley shortly before her body was found there. He was an outsider and not known to the townspeople.
为了极力找出弗里达的凶手，当地人举行了一场降神会。在20世纪20年代，人们普遍认为这种行为可以与可能提供关键信息的灵魂进行交流。据一位参与者称，降神会成功了，灵魂们对外貌进行了描述，这与弗里达的谋杀犯相符。这个描述恰好与在她尸体被发现前不久被看到在小巷附近徘徊的一个男子的外貌相吻合。他是个外地人，镇民们都不认识他。

9
00:05:37.000 --> 00:06:28.000
From 30 to 40 years of age, approximately 5 feet 6 inches tall, with dark hair and a heavy mustache. He was wearing dark breeches, a lounge coat and carrying a stick. The information obtained via the seance was taken seriously at the time, but local authorities sought further evidence. This type of crime was unheard of in arbitrary and was beyond their expertise, so they requested assistance from London's experienced and well-equipped Scotland Yard Police Force. Two detectives soon arrived in town to carry out an investigation.
年龄在30到40岁之间，身高约5英尺6英寸，留着深色头发和浓密的胡须。他穿着深色马裤、休闲西装外套，手里拿着一根棍子。通过降神会获得的信息在当时受到了重视，但地方当局寻求更多的证据。这种类型的犯罪在阿伯泰勒里闻所未闻，超出了他们的专业范围，因此他们请求伦敦经验丰富且装备精良的苏格兰场警察部队协助。两名侦探不久便抵达镇上开展调查。

10
00:06:28.000 --> 00:07:09.000
It was determined that Freedah was murdered between 9.30am and 1pm on the day she went missing. Her body was found in close proximity to a shed used by Mortimer's store, which contained stock too large to fit on the shop floor. Multiple witnesses said that shortly after Freedah left Mortimer's, they heard screams coming from the direction of the storage shed, but assumed it was just children playing. A resident who lived near the building heard what she described as a muffled, funny-sounding argument between 9.20 and 9.30am.
经确定，弗里达是在她失踪当天的上午9点30分至下午1点之间被谋杀的。她的尸体被发现在靠近莫蒂默商店的一个棚屋附近，该棚屋里存放着太大而无法放入店面的存货。多名目击者称，在弗里达离开莫蒂默后不久，他们听到储藏室方向传来尖叫声，但以为只是小孩子在玩耍。一名住在该建筑附近的居民听到她形容为在9点20分到9点30分之间听起来很滑稽的、闷声闷气的争吵。

11
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:54.000
She thought it was her son in the backyard hurting one of their chickens, but when she headed outside to check, she found her son playing in a nearby lane. On the floor of the Mortimer's shed were loose pieces of corn chaff, matching shards recovered from Freedah's skin and the sack she was found in. A small handkerchief that Freedah was carrying the day she was attacked was also discovered in the shed, as was an axe. It was hidden under a sack, and while the blade itself was clean, the handle was covered in wet blood.
她以为是自己的儿子在后院弄伤了他们的鸡，但当她走出去查看时，发现她的儿子正在附近的巷子里玩耍。莫蒂默棚屋的地上有碎玉米壳，这与从弗里达皮肤上以及发现她的麻袋中回收的碎片相吻合。弗里达遭受袭击当天随身携带的一块小手帕也在棚屋里被发现，一把斧头也是如此。它藏在一个麻袋下面，虽然斧刃本身很干净，但斧柄上沾满了湿血。

12
00:07:54.000 --> 00:08:38.000
The shed was 275m from Mortimer's store, which was owned and operated by its namesake, a local man named Herbert Mortimer. Herbert had a strong alibi for the day of Freedah's murder, with multiple witnesses confirming his whereabouts at the time she was attacked. As for his storage shed, Herbert revealed that it was kept locked at all times, and that there were only two keys that granted access. Herbert carried one. The other was held by one of his employees, 15-year-old Harold Jones.
该棚屋距离莫蒂默商店275米，该商店由同名的当地人赫伯特·莫蒂默（Herbert Mortimer）拥有和经营。赫伯特对弗里达被谋杀那天有强有力不在场证明，多名目击者证实了她在遭受袭击时的行踪。至于他的储藏室，赫伯特透露，它一直处于锁闭状态，只有两把钥匙可以进入。赫伯特随身携带一把。另一把由他的一个员工、15岁的哈罗德·琼斯（Harold Jones）保管。

13
00:08:38.000 --> 00:09:22.000
Harold was at the front counter when Freedah visited Mortimer's on February 5. She arrived shortly after 9am, and only spent around two minutes in the store. Harold didn't notice which direction she headed in upon exiting the shop. Herbert Mortimer vouched for his young staff member, telling detectives that Harold Jones was at the store nearly all morning. Herbert's wife supported this assertion. She had been in their apartment above the shop, and could hear Harold banging his foot against the wood paneling of the counter, something he did constantly as he walked.
2月5日弗里达光顾莫蒂默时，哈罗德正在前台。她刚过9点到达，在店里只呆了大约两分钟。哈罗德没有注意到她出店后朝哪个方向走去。赫伯特·莫蒂默为他的年轻员工作担保，告诉侦探哈罗德·琼斯几乎整个上午都在店里。赫伯特的妻子证实了这一说法。她一直在楼上的公寓里，能听到哈罗德用脚踢柜台的木镶板，这是他走路时经常做的一个动作。

14
00:09:22.000 --> 00:10:02.000
According to Herbert, Harold only left once for a short period at 10am, almost an hour after Freedah Bernal had stopped by. He'd been tasked with retrieving some stock from the shed, but the teenager didn't go alone. Herbert's 10-year-old son Francis joined him. The pair made the short walk together, collected a sack of potatoes from the shed, and delivered them to a nearby address before returning to the store. Later that day, when word spread that Freedah Bernal was missing, Harold slid his hand into
据赫伯特说，哈罗德在上午10点左右只离开了一小会儿，几乎是在弗里达·伯内尔离开一小时后。他被派去从棚屋取回一些存货，但这个少年并不是一个人去的。赫伯特10岁的儿子弗朗西斯（Francis）加入了他的行列。两人一起短距离步行，从棚屋里取出一袋土豆，将它们送到附近的地址，然后返回店里。那天晚些时候，当弗里达·伯内尔失踪的消息传开时，哈罗德把手伸进

15
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:45.000
his pocket, only to realise that he didn't have the key to the shed on him. Then dawned that he must have left it in the shed's door after running the errand with Francis Mortimer hours earlier. Harold kept news of the misplaced key to himself, avoiding the fuss that would arise if his employer knew of his mistake. Later on, while helping look for Freedah, Harold went back to the shed with Francis Mortimer and another local team, and was able to retrieve the key. He didn't notice anything suspicious around the building at the time.
他的口袋，却意识到身上没有棚屋的钥匙。随后他恍然大悟，一定是几个小时前和弗朗西斯·莫蒂默一起跑腿时把它忘在棚屋门上了。哈罗德对钥匙放错地方的消息闭口不谈，以免让雇主知道他的错误而引起大惊小怪。后来，在帮忙寻找弗里达时，哈罗德和弗朗西斯·莫蒂默以及另一个当地团队回到了棚屋，并成功找回了钥匙。当时他没有注意到大楼周围有什么可疑之处。

16
00:10:45.000 --> 00:11:23.000
Harold's story of leaving the key in the shed door opened the investigation up to many potential suspects. Anyone could have taken Freedah into the secluded building upon realising it was accessible. Yet, despite having a strong alibi, Harold Jones was eyed by Scotland Yard as a prime suspect in the case. The 15-year-old knew Freedah Bernal personally, as she was friends with his little sister, Flossie. Consequently, a level of trust existed between Harold and Freedah, which meant he could have
哈罗德把钥匙落在棚屋门上的说法，让这项调查牵扯出许多潜在的嫌疑人。任何人一旦意识到该建筑可以进入，都可能把弗里达带进这个偏僻的建筑里。然而，尽管有强有力的不在场证明，哈罗德·琼斯还是被苏格兰场视为该案的主要嫌疑人。这个15岁的男孩认识弗里达·伯内尔，因为她是他的小妹妹弗洛西（Flossie）的朋友。因此，哈罗德和弗里达之间存在一定程度的信任，这意味着他可以

17
00:11:23.000 --> 00:12:04.000
easily convinced her to go to the shed. The alleyway where she was later found had been searched the night she vanished, but the sack containing her remains was not spotted at that time. Investigators suspected Harold had returned to the shed in the early hours and removed Freedah's body under the cover of darkness, before dumping it in the alley where it was discovered the following day. But none of this made sense to Abitaliri's residence. Jones' employers vouched for his whereabouts at the time Freedah was attacked.
轻而易举地劝说她去棚屋。她后来被发现的小巷在她失踪当晚就被搜查过，但当时并没有发现装着她遗体的麻袋。调查人员怀疑哈罗德在清晨返回棚屋，在夜色的掩护下转移了弗里达的尸体，然后将其扔进第二天被发现的小巷里。但这一切在阿伯泰勒里居民看来都说不通。琼斯的老板为弗里达遇袭时的行踪作了担保。

18
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:55.000
Furthermore, Harold's parents insisted that their son had been home all night. As a means of obtaining additional income, the Jones family hosted a border who, due to a lack of space, actually slept in Harold's bed alongside him. The border maintained that Harold had remained in their shared bed all night. Despite the town coming to his support, Harold Jones was arrested on suspicion of Freedah Bernal's murder and held at the Abitaliri police station to await an inquest into the eight-year-old's death. He adamantly denied any knowledge of the crime.
此外，哈罗德的父母坚称他们的儿子一整晚都在家。为了获得额外收入，琼斯一家接待了一名房客，由于空间不足，他实际上和哈罗德睡在同一张床上。房客坚称哈罗德一整晚都呆在他们共用的床上。尽管全镇都来支持他，哈罗德·琼斯仍因涉嫌谋杀弗里达·伯内尔而被捕，并被关押在阿伯泰勒里警察局，等待对这名八岁女孩死因的死因研讯。他坚决否认自己知道这起罪行。

19
00:12:55.000 --> 00:13:39.000
The grief that had washed over Abitaliri following the murder was quickly replaced by outrage over the arrest of Harold, who was an exemplary young lad. Like many others in the community, he came from a coal mining family. The working-class Joneses made do with what they had and were immensely proud of their eldest son, Harold, who was intelligent and well-read. He was very much loved by his parents, Philip and Eleanor, and neither he nor anyone in his family had any previous run-ins with the law. Harold was an inquisitive youth and had done very well at school, with his former principal
谋杀案后笼罩阿伯泰勒里的悲痛，很快就被对逮捕哈罗德的愤怒所取代，他是一个堪称楷模的年轻小伙。和社区里的许多人一样，他来自一个煤矿工人家庭。工人阶级的琼斯一家有什么就用什么，并为他们聪明好学的大儿子哈罗德感到无比自豪。他的父母菲利普（Philip）和埃莉诺（Eleanor）非常疼爱他，他和他的家人以前都没有过违法记录。哈罗德是一个充满好奇心的青年，在学校表现非常好，他的前校长

20
00:13:39.000 --> 00:14:20.000
describing him as a model student. He loved to play the organ and practiced regularly at home. Harold left school at age 14, which was common at the time. He avoided taking up work in the physically demanding and dangerous coal mines by securing a job as a shop boy for mortemers. To mark his new employment, Harold had a photo taken of himself standing outside the store. It showed the slight teen immaculately dressed in a suit, complete with pocket watch and cap.
形容他是一个模范学生。他喜欢弹风琴，经常在家练习。哈罗德14岁时辍学，这在当时很常见。他通过保住一份为莫蒂默当店员的工作，避免了从事体力要求高且危险的煤矿工作。为了纪念他的新工作，哈罗德拍了一张自己站在店外面的照片。照片显示这个瘦削的少年衣着无可挑剔，穿着西装，配有怀表和帽子。

21
00:14:20.000 --> 00:15:03.000
Not one to have his photo taken often, Harold stood awkwardly before the camera, which captured his blank expression. Herbert Mortimer said Harold was an obedient and trustworthy employee, which was why he gave him a key to his storage shed. Harold took great pride in his appearance, wearing a suit and clean white apron to work every day, and his friendly nature ensured he was well liked by customers. Outside of work, the popular Harold was never short of friends and had started dating a girl just prior to his arrest.
哈罗德不常拍照，他在镜头前显得很不自然，脸上带着茫然的表情。赫伯特·莫蒂默说，哈罗德是一个听话且值得信赖的员工，这就是为什么他给了他一把储藏室的钥匙。哈罗德对自己的外表感到非常自豪，每天上班都穿着西装和干净的白色围裙，他友善的性格确保了他深受顾客喜爱。工作之余，受欢迎的哈罗德从不缺朋友，并在被捕前不久开始和一个女孩约会。

22
00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:47.000
Still, the investigators from Scotland Yard were certain they had Frida's killer in custody. Local police supported their decision, much to the fury of the public. They knew an outsider was to blame. A coroner's inquest into the death of Frida Bernal formally began a month after she was found. Harold's purpose was to determine whether Frida's death was caused by willful murder, and if so, whether Harold Jones would face a criminal trial. Due to a lack of scientific testing at the time, the evidence against Harold was largely
尽管如此，苏格兰场的调查人员确信他们已经拘留了弗里达的凶手。当地警方支持他们的决定，这引发了公众的极大愤怒。他们知道罪魁祸首是一个外地人。在弗里达·伯内尔被发现一个月后，对她死因的验尸官研讯正式开始。哈罗德的目的是确定弗里达的死是否是由蓄意谋杀引起的，如果是的话，哈罗德·琼斯是否将面临刑事审判。由于当时缺乏科学检测手段，对哈罗德不利的证据主要是

