00:15:47.000 --> 00:16:31.000
circumstantial. Harold had spent the past month in a prison cell at Aberteleiri police station. From taking the witness box, he looked nervous and had difficulty answering questions, often giving contradictory evidence. The prosecution took his anxious demeanour as a sign of guilt, and for four hours they continued to barrage him with questions. Multiple people testified in Harold's defence, including his employer, his parents, and the border who shared his bed, all in turn providing crucial alibis.
